# Finite local ladder with unchanged global free dynamics

## Verdict and distinct conservation scope

The proposed second construction is valid: retain the entire native matter
system and its full global free Hamiltonian, localize/round ONLY the event
fibers, then discretize and cap the shared battery. It gives a finite positive
battery apparatus approximating the globally free local-continuous-jump law,
and can be composed with the earlier locality estimate. Exact rounded GLOBAL
energy conservation does not follow and is not asserted. This is distinct from
the matched finite-patch theorem in FINITE_LADDER_APPROXIMATION.md.

## Physical local controls, not global-history measurements

Write the free system Hamiltonian as Aglob on the native matter/head/fuel/Record
space. It preserves the declared classical head/fuel sector projectors and acts
trivially on the degenerate history labels. For each legal oriented edge e,
let E_e be its head-and-live-fuel legality effect, and K_e the complete sign
column, K_e*K_e=E_e. At most D edges are legal on any source sector.

Choose a ball B_R containing the entire physical support of K_e, its head/fuel
transition and the deleted hopping. Truncate full local interaction TERMS by
support to obtain Ain,R and Aout,R. For all included source patterns require
 Hrem,out,R K_e=K_e Hrem,in,R, and ||h_e||<=t.
Then the local transfer defect is at most c=Delta+t. These are the same ambient
native-algebra assumptions as before, checked termwise on surviving physical
hoppings. A CAR-only matrix identification does not prove this property.

The controlled local Hamiltonians may depend on fuel/Record patterns INSIDE
B_R. Implement that control with local pattern projectors; all other source
sectors see the same local operator tensored with identity outside B_R. Rounding
each local pattern block spectrally keeps this support. Include all local
patterns, not a selected favorable global history. Updating the head, selected
fuel and Record label is injective on the remaining source-pattern labels;
retain distinct sign/direction channel labels so column norms do not acquire
coherent interference between different source patterns.

A mathematical direct-sum decomposition by global histories may be used to
prove uniform bounds, but must not be implemented as a physical projector
measuring the entire history. A fine-grained generator with separate global-
history environment labels can dephase history coherences differently from a
local grouped generator. Equivalence on arbitrary coherent histories requires
an actual proof; alternatively restrict the comparison input to the supplied
initial definite-history sector, whose jump process remains a classical mixture.
The locality claim applies to genuinely locally controlled jumps, not to an
unjustified replacement of a globally measuring instrument.

## Local rounding and complete effects

Round the local block eigenvalues to delta Z, preserving their projectors, so
||Ain,R-Ain,R^delta|| and ||Aout,R-Aout,R^delta|| are <=delta/2. Use full local
fuel energies once, or a compatible mesh preserving Delta separately. Define
 W_R(tau)=exp(-i tau Aout,R)K_e exp(i tau Ain,R),
 W_R^delta(tau)=exp(-i tau Aout,R^delta)K_e exp(i tau Ain,R^delta).
The local input blocks commute with their legality effect E_e. Thus BOTH
columns have effect E_e, and
 ||W_R(tau)-W_R^delta(tau)||<=delta|tau|,
 ||[EB^delta,W_R^delta]||<=c+delta.                       (1)
The latter follows by adding the two local spectral-rounding errors to the
local transfer defect. It does not require rounded surviving terms still to
commute individually with K_e. Different local truncations for different edges
cause no problem: each has the same corresponding legality effect E_e.

Because E_e depends on conserved head/fuel data, it commutes with the full
Aglob. The total outgoing effect is R=gamma sum_e E_e<=gamma D I. Uniformization
at Lambda=gamma D therefore has the same null block in both laws. In fact
Fourier marginal transport below only needs trace preservation, but this effect
identity makes the unchanged rate/degree interpretation explicit.

## Finite ladder, keeping global matter untouched

Embed ladder level j as the normalized constant function on
[j delta,(j+1)delta), with battery energy E_j=(j+1/2)delta. Let
EB^delta(E)=delta(floor(E/delta)+1/2).
Rounded local differences are integer delta shifts, so W_R^delta preserves the
step-function battery subspace. The unchanged Aglob acts only on the system
and also preserves that subspace. Replace ONLY free EB by EB^delta; then the
full free Hamiltonian is Aglob+EB^delta. No global matter spectrum is rounded.
Its free propagation commutes strongly with EB^delta and its cap projection,
although it generally does not commute with the local jumps.

For C=M delta retain j=0,...,M-1, all strictly positive. Cap each combined edge
column once and add F_e=(E_e-S_e*S_e)^(1/2) into an absorbing refusal sector.
The effect identity restores E_e and hence the exact original degree rate,
while every matrix acting on matter is still supported within B_R: functional
calculus for F_e occurs on the same local matter tensor factor and finite
battery. No external global-history projector is introduced by this square
root. The refusing state then evolves with the stipulated full free Aglob on
its absorbing copy, with physical outgoing jumps disabled.

This is a finite-dimensional battery apparatus of M levels plus a refusal flag.
The original global matter Hilbert space is NOT replaced by a local d-dimensional
patch. Total dimension is at most2 d_global M when the global finite native
system dimension is d_global; additional storage capacity is ceil(log2 M)+1
qubits. This is a capacity count, not an explicit locality-preserving hardware
encoding or synthesis of the bath. Existing head/fuel/Record resources remain.

## Why the Fourier comparison still works

Before EB is discretized or capped, both globally free laws have jumps that
multiply in tau and free Hamiltonian Aglob-i partial_tau. Their dissipators
annihilate every multiplication projector1_B(tau), regardless of whether the
jumps intertwine Aglob+EB. Therefore p_t(tau)=p_0(tau-t) in BOTH laws, including
correlated system/battery states. Energy covariance is not needed for this
marginal identity. An arbitrary untouched reference is allowed.

On the initial band|tau0|<=Tcut and interval[0,T], the column difference from
local rounding is bounded by delta(Tcut+t). The same bounded-generator
calculation as before gives integrated jump-channel error
 4Lambda delta(T Tcut+T²/2).
Changing only EB to EB^delta costs delta T in diamond norm, because its bounded
operator difference is <=delta/2. There is NO free-A rounding term here.
The EB change is handled after the Fourier-band comparison by a separate
bounded-perturbation estimate; pure Fourier transport is not assumed after it.

## Explicit retained-output bound and composition

Initial beta is sine on[b,b+w], b>0, with u=C-b-w>0. Its normalized cell
projection beta_delta costs at most2delta/w in initial trace norm. Let
 eta<=32pi/[3(w Tcut)^3], Tcut>=sqrt(2)pi/w,
 lambda=Lambda T, P(lambda)=lambda+(3/2)lambda²+(1/3)lambda³,
 B_delta=(c+delta)²[(b-delta/2)^-2+(u-delta/2)^-2]P(lambda),
with delta<min(w,b,u).
The local-continuous globally free process and the finite-ladder capped one
then satisfy
 distance<=min{2,
  2delta/w+4Lambda delta(T Tcut+T²/2)+delta T
                  +4sqrt(eta)+4sqrt(B_delta)}.           (2)
The last term is the repeated-intermediate-cap bound, not final leakage used
as first-exit probability. It remains valid because free Aglob+EB^delta commutes
with EB^delta and the uniformized rounded local column obeys(1). Poisson ticks
are interleaved with actual global free propagation. Null ticks neither move
battery energy nor create extra refusal on an accepted state.

If the exact global lift and the local continuous lift obey the uniform
finite-time locality hypothesis
 ||W_global(tau)-W_R(tau)||
 <=epsilon_R=C_R exp[-mu(R-a-v(Tcut+T))]
on the enlarged band and every required history, a direct common-band comparison
gives the stronger composed estimate
 distance(Exact_global,Finite_local_ladder)
 <=min{2,2delta/w+4Lambda T epsilon_R
       +4Lambda delta(T Tcut+T²/2)+delta T
       +4sqrt(eta)+4sqrt(B_delta)}.                      (3)
Only one Fourier-tail term is needed when applying the common-band proof to
the SUM of locality and rounding column errors. Applying the two separate
triangle inequalities is also valid but pays the tail twice. Equation(3)
keeps global matter/free propagation and the original initial matter input.

The target-epsilon recipe of the matched-patch memo applies with its error
coefficient replaced by
 Aerr=2/w+4Lambda(T Tcut+T²/2)+T,
and a separately allocated locality budget4Lambda T epsilon_R. The cap term
still requires an explicit margin check; fixed cap leakage is not eliminated
by mesh refinement. All parameters are theoretical resource variables, not a
retuning of a frozen science fixture.

## Energy statement: exact conservation is intentionally absent

The local-rounded lift intertwines Ain,R^delta+EB^delta with Aout,R^delta+EB^delta.
The process uses Aglob+EB^delta as its free Hamiltonian. These are different
system operators, so neither accepted jumps nor refusal complements need
intertwine GLOBAL total energy. Cap completion ensures CPTP and the original
degree effect, not global energy covariance. The original matched-patch mean
energy bound3delta+2delta²/w cannot be copied to this model.

A separate energy analysis would have to bound the total-energy defect for
every relevant column, AND the refusal-channel generator contribution:
 (Aglob,out+EB^delta)W_R^delta-W_R^delta(Aglob,in+EB^delta).
The local exact-lift relation cancels local rounded terms; what remains includes
commutators with boundary-crossing global interactions and local rounding errors.
Distant terms with disjoint support cancel, so a separate local boundary estimate
may be feasible, but it is not automatically small and must include F_e. A small
trace error against an unbounded global energy observable does not replace this
calculation. No physical global-energy error is asserted in(2)–(3).

## Scope

This construction composes finite-neighborhood jump approximation with a finite
positive battery while retaining the full global free matter dynamics. It is an
explicit finite-dimensional GKSL apparatus model, still using a supplied Markov
reservoir, preparation, memory and local spectral controls. It does not derive
native one-site/Z3 admissibility, a local bath Hamiltonian, entropy reset,
closed-unitary implementation or renewal. Completeness, legal local controls
and uniform all-history locality estimates remain the stated prerequisites.
